{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462901-build-a-mage-to-fight-an-antediluvian","id":1462901,"title":"Build a Mage to fight an Antediluvian","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-06T11:10:46-07:00","id":1462901,"title":"Build a Mage to fight an Antediluvian","content":"I am in a long running WOD campaign that is a mix of mage and vampire PCs. Everyone is powerful. (IE: 4th gen vampires, archmages) - this has been running for years and we started as humans. I'm a mage. We have encountered two antediluvians in our travels and the coterie/cabal/whatever has a pretty good relationship with one and an escalating relationship with the other (Set, who is... currently not able to take direct actions). I think we are about to tangle with others or see changes as we are approaching the time of the Camarilla / Tremere / etc. It's in the 1100s. <br /> <br /> Anyway, forgetting for a moment whether you think this is insane or not (it's fun, we've played together for 20 years, so we're ok with this game structure which would obviously be OP/nuts for others)...<br /> <br /> How would you build a mage to fight an antediluvian?<br /> <br /> The following special advantages exist:<br /> * Paradox is extremely low in this time period / environment. <br /> * Fast casting / on the fly casting is largely possible. (This is a pretty loose interpretation of the mage rules..)<br /> * Maybe assume 1 6 dot sphere, 2-3 5 dot spheres, 1-2 4 dot spheres. And Arete, Avatar 7+.<br /> <br /> I have Arete 8. There will likely be several vampires with 1-2 disciplines in the 8-9 range in the fight. If we are forced to fight an antediluvian it will likely be Set, although Tremere and Tzimisce are also possible.<br /> <br /> I am not sure we can win, so the strategy might also be a fight to escape / stalemate / imprison.<br /> <br /> Looking forward to your thoughts!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26423-lokitx","name":"LokiTX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T11:23:54-07:00","id":1462905,"title":"","content":"All you need is Matter 5/Prime 2/Time 2. One of the characteristics of Matter 5 is that it allows you to create material with any properties you like. Time 2 looks into the future and reveals what type of material kills the Antediluvian, and Matter 5/Prime 2 then creates that material around the Antediluvian. Done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T11:34:55-07:00","id":1462908,"title":"","content":"So....<br /> <br /> 1) The biggest issue is that we don't have stats for Antes to build against. The Antes are walking plot devices that are as potent as the writers/ST deem. As such it's basically impossible to mechanically suggest ways to beat them because it's hard to know what your ST will consider them capable of.<br /> <br /> 2) That said, preparation is always a mage's biggest advantage. Esp. when it comes to archmages existing in a time of little Paradox concerns, you should probably have a suit of prepped effects where single reflexive action (even one your PC isn't consciously aware of) actives an potent effect relevant to the sudden threat. Hulking out in physical combat is obvious, but things like having a whole Demense dream fortress prepped that any magical mental intrusions cause you and the offender to be sent to your own private dreamscape where you control the rules for a mind-to-mind fight is also something for an example to be ready for; esp. with vampires.<br /> <br /> 3) Your second biggest advantage is going to be group ritual castings. Not sure what rules you're using exactly, but if your PC group have enough of a shared style, or you've amassed enough apprentices and/or cult member in service to you, you can get a huge boost to your magical casting. Having five apprentices that can't cast what you can, but have the base Spheres you do, means +5 successes on each of your ritual rolls. So this means your prepped magic get real strong real fast.<br /> <br /> 4) The only real example in the books of what this looks like is Voormas in Ascension (the End Times book for Revised). The stats for fighting Voormas are insane, and they're for him when he's <b>distracted</b> doing his big world ending ritual. Because fighting him any other time is insta-death for anyone not on his level (and he outclasses the presumed stats you posted, he can beat archmages like Senex if a fair fight... which is why Senex has never let that happen).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T12:23:18-07:00","id":1462915,"title":"","content":"I would want Time 4 or higher so that I could pause time and avoid the antediluvian having any chance to act. If you are facing an adversary with such power, any opportunity they have to use one of their high level disciplines could be instant death for the whole party.<br /> <br /> To actually Find the enemy, who may have incredibly high Obfuscate, I would want Correspondence, Mind and Entropy to break through the illusion - Memory's Fading Glimpse, for example. Since there is already a story established in which you know some antediluvians and have met at least one, you are already considered to be above the effect that purges the target from memory.<br /> <br /> Prime 5 so that you have as much Quintessence as you need to lower the difficulty of high level multi-sphere spells.<br /> <br /> Combine your Prime 5 with whatever level of Forces is needed to deliver effects that inflict Aggravated damage (It might have to take the form of fire, for example).<br /> <br /> I would say Correspondence should be one of your level 4s to cover every variation of delivering an effect from a distance.<br /> <br /> Cast multiple effects with Time 4 Contingency that all go off all at once, ensuring he has absolutely no way to react. He is incinerated.<br /> <br /> Other ideas:<br /> <br /> Correspondence 5, Matter 3, Forces 5 to blend his location with that of an active volcano. It's not targeted at him, so any Disciplines that would resist can be bypassed by targeting the location.<br /> <br /> Another idea would not be to destroy but to capture the antediluvian and gain control of him. If he's sleeping, he will have to feed when he wakes up and probably has some plan in place so that he has a supply of blood when he wakes up. With Life, Matter, Prime and Mind, you could enchant blood so that it functions like a drug. Keep him addicted to a drug that facilitates your troupe influencing him. If he's awake, use the aforementioned Time 4 and Correspondence to target the blood he's drinking when he feeds, from a safe distance.<br /> <br /> You could try to use the Vampire's own high level Auspex against him. Compare it too blasting sonic waves at a highly sensitive receiver. With Mind, Spirit, Correspondence and Entropy, force him to peer into something like a Nephandi Labyrinth (or equally complex thing in the universe that avoids turning the antediluvian into an infernalist who is more dangerous).<br /> <br /> Good luck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 10-06-2021, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T13:00:01-07:00","id":1462922,"title":"","content":"The only thing about this I find problematic it's that the capabilities of an Ante are entirely STfiat, and thus there's no real answer outside of what your ST wants to happen.<br /> <br /> But I think it's worth while to speculate what could be cool or interesting ways to approach such a feat, and what has been done in the Lore to do it.<br /> <br /> One could speculate about the amount of firepower that took to kill an Ante in the canon (nukes + sunligth) to estimate the amount you need to bring (in a Mage book it was suggested the OoH could replicate the nuking of Ravnos by summoning a meteorite to stop him, for instance)<br /> <br /> Or about the Lore of that specific vampire:<br /> *Set may or may not be fused with Apophis, making him more spirit than vampire (if that entity can be said to be a spirit) - because permanently killing such a being may well be impossible even for your regular Arch-dude, imprisonment could work better.<br /> *Set may or may not be in a cold war with his own Bane Mummies, who may or may not know his True Name (could be relevant for some forms of magick) - so you may have insider help if you're willing to make some nasty deals.<br /> *Seek the aid of Horus/Osiris (that fought him in the past)<br /> *I don't know much about egyptian mitology, but if you study the way Set was killed/injured there (I think Thoth made a special spear for Horus), that may provide a Bonus<br /> <br /> But, ultimately, it really depends on how your table does things.<br /> <br /> Personaly, I would approach this not as a Rote but as a Story - a certain amount of steps would need to be taken to bring the beast coser to it's demise, more than a single spell. Magick that vampires *normaly* don't have defense against, like Time/Space manipulation, might not be so unilaterally effective. In that sense, no single &quot;build&quot; would do the trick (albeit some could certainly help).<br /> <br /> But maybe your table it's different, and you need to be able to do X amount of Aggravated Damage, have &quot;soul extintion&quot; powers to erase it's spirit, prepare a spell to teleport the ante to the sun, or some other combination of combat mechanics that I can only speculate on. Maybe the ST already finished the Ante's charsheet, and you just need to beat/sidestep whatever's in there.<br /> <br /> If you have to flee, I would recommend fleeing to an &quot;Heaven-like&quot; place where the Ante wouldn't be welcomed. Like, in the case of Set, the court of Ra comes to mind<br /> <br /> But, again, if any of this works would depend heavily on your ST's intentions. If you're not sure you can win, much less I. Soo ... try to bring in as much power as you can (have defeated Methuselah before? - well, bring in more power than when you did that), taste the waters before jump\u00edng, and be prepared to flee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-06-2021, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T13:38:09-07:00","id":1462928,"title":"","content":"Same answer I gave in another topic, I think you must learn more. Instead of thinking a build to fight an Ante, make a build to gather information on an Ante.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T15:17:40-07:00","id":1462936,"title":"","content":"So this is all awesome, let me provide some more details based on the replies.<br /> <br /> Definitely get the ST take. I think in our case this it is probably up to us how we approach it. We have a ton of information already and continue to gather it as we expect to go to war with Set at some point. We've killed several of his childer and many of his grand-childer. We have met him in a spirit realm and have been warned that he is after us.<br /> <br /> I asked with a lot of open ended-ness because I was just curious. <br /> <br /> Right now my mage is Prime 6, Spirit 5, Forces/Life/Mind/Correspondence 3, and everything else is 2. I have enough XP to buy one of those 3 spheres to a 4 (or I could move to of the 2s to 3s in another few sessions). But things are pretty expensive and I'm trying to strategy. So was looking to see what people thought sphere wise and maybe get more thoughts on how to use the spheres against something of ante power.<br /> <br /> Also one of the vampires has at least Temporis 8 (maybe 9), so we have some pretty significant time manipulation powers already.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26423-lokitx","name":"LokiTX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T15:25:47-07:00","id":1462938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiTX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462901-build-a-mage-to-fight-an-antediluvian#post1462901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, forgetting for a moment whether you think this is insane or not (it's fun, we've played together for 20 years, so we're ok with this game structure which would obviously be OP/nuts for others)...<br /> <br /> How would you build a mage to fight an antediluvian?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462901-build-a-mage-to-fight-an-antediluvian?p=1462922#post1462922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personaly, I would approach this not as a Rote but as a Story - a certain amount of steps would need to be taken to bring the beast coser to it's demise, more than a single spell. Magick that vampires *normaly* don't have defense against, like Time/Space manipulation, might not be so unilaterally effective. In that sense, no single &quot;build&quot; would do the trick (albeit some could certainly help).</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462901-build-a-mage-to-fight-an-antediluvian?p=1462928#post1462928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same answer I gave in another topic, I think you must learn more. Instead of thinking a build to fight an Ante, make a build to gather information on an Ante.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question seems to have shifted from &quot;How do super-Mages take down an unspecified antediluvian if we allocate the right Spheres?&quot; to &quot;What's an innovative and dramatically rich way the players can use their characters to drive the story in the direction of defeating/destroying a single antediluvian?&quot;. It's interesting to ponder both, but a third question might add some helpful context; &quot;Which specific antediluvian?&quot; (I finally spelled the word without having to copy-paste) Each antediluvian will have a different set of resistances and powers, as well as a unique role in the Vampire Metaplot/ Lore. A death fitting one might not suit another or be possible due to different powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T16:37:30-07:00","id":1462941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiTX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462901-build-a-mage-to-fight-an-antediluvian?p=1462936#post1462936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right now my mage is Prime 6, Spirit 5, Forces/Life/Mind/Correspondence 3, and everything else is 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Buy Mind.<br /> <br /> Set is a master of Obfuscate and Presence, both powers that rely heavily on Mind to affect others in an area. You may have to ease the burden on the Mind master of the group to protect you and be able to extend protection to others, PCs and NPCs alike. Outside some fear effects Serpentis is a more personal power for a vampire and won't change the strategy that much, just make him tougher.<br /> <br /> Also be prepared to fight him more than once, as Serpentis also gives him Lich-like powers where he can sacrifice himself and just return again if you can't locate his true heart (if it even still exists as such).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T18:44:25-07:00","id":1462951,"title":"","content":"If it's in the 1100s and you are facing the God of Darkness, where is the sun in the cosmology? This is before the Void Engineers fortified the Gauntlet, before we came to view things in terms of a solar system with planets. If you have Spirit 5, can you not make a gate between the sun, wherever it is in the Umbra, and an earthly location? Add your Prime and Forces and make portal that shines pure solar light in one direction so that you can stand behind it unharmed. It is a fitting end for Set.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you could add Life and anchor the effect to your own body so that intense sunlight radiates from you, making it impossible for Set to face or approach you. With Matter, anchor it to an object. Actually...<br /> <br /> If you have Prime 2, you can enchant an object with an effect.<br /> <br /> With Corr2, Matter 2, you can teleport an object (to Set).<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> got into some of the mythology behind why Vampires are vulnerable to sunlight. This is a copy-paste rather than using quote button, since it is from another post (of mine), <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419152-tolerating-vampires-reasons-to-magick-tactics-and-infiltrating-them\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...iltrating-them</a> <br /> <br /> Koronos said, &quot;Remind me of a head canon why sunlight is deadly to vampires but other light like from lightnings or torches not.<br /> It is actually a cooperation of Jahwe, Gaia and Helios. Jahwe asked Gaia, if she can make it, that, as long those that exist because of Caines cursed blood are within her realms, Helios light is a deadly poisen for them.<br /> So Helios light alone would contain some godly resonance that allone would be harmless and is only in the light of helios but in combination of Gaias sphere it will change into something very dangerous. So Vampire in space looking into the sun, ok.<br /> Vampire being on Earth looking into an UV lamp, not very pleasuring but no problem either.<br /> Vampire standing on Moon, Mars or other planet while being day? The problem would be more if the atmosphere is damaging the body.<br /> But being on earth while day makes the sun to something deadly.&quot;<br /> <br /> With Spirit 5, you could try to call on the power of Gaia and Helios.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T07:33:18-07:00","id":1463310,"title":"","content":"Fight an Antediluvian? Not try to combat Antediluvian's influence, plots, or their agents, not try to stalk an Antediluvian in their place of rest (also a folly, I'll come back to this later), but try to fight one directly? Oh dear, I just think this cannot work. The way I see it, the original 3rd Generation Founders just have this privilege that they cannot be simply harmed directly, except by each other. Their physical bodies are too resistant, their mysticism too potent, and their combat stats (including regeneration ability) are too high. Even the battle forms of Mages (be it the mystical ones Traditions have listed or the Hard Suits of the Technocracy) are simply not powerful enough.<br /> <br /> There is also another factor - did you know that many Disciplines have higher level Powers that allow for instant disabling or kill? Dominate has Still the Mortal Flesh, Auspex has Psychic Assault, Obtenebration has the Darkness Within, and Dementation has Personal Scourge. Just on the possibility of an Antediluvian having one of them or a similar one, attacking one directly is a folly. Even if such a Power is not known, then simply using Dread Gaze, Majesty, Mesmerize, or Celerity might end the fight before it has really began. Remember that those Powers are used with full weight of an Antediluvian's potency (so possibility of traits of 7-10, in terms of mechanics).<br /> <br /> In regard to using Spells, I'm thinking that even a fully loaded destruction Spell wouldn't be enough to disable or destroy a being like an Antediluvian. Also consider that in setting, actions do not happen in a single instance like in the rules for casting Magic. There is gonna be a need to assume a posture, speak some words, channel power through Foci etc. While this is going on an Antediluvian can move in for the kill or to disable. Also, considering who they are, I'm thinking at least some of them could Unweave Spells and Rituals used against them. Or use some item or speak an ancient secret, that disables spellcasting around them.<br /> <br /> Just to go through some specific Antediluvians...<br /> <br /> The most suited to fighting Mages seems to be Arikel - who would think so, considering she is the Toreador Founder? But it makes sense, she was known as Ishtar, goddess of love and war, after all. With mastery of Celerity, Presence, and Auspex, she seems the most powerful in regard to taking out vulnerable and flighty targets like Mages, including multiple ones. The scariest part is that she could probably Entrance some of the attackers mid-combat. And even if some would survive, then due to meeting Arikel they would be vulnerable to being Summoned by her in the future...<br /> <br /> Ennoia - I just do not see the point of challenging her at all. With mastery of Fortitude and Protean she probably can resist damage the best out of the Antediluvian's. Also Animalism can affect mortals at higher levels, and she could have animal servants for additional defense and distraction.<br /> <br /> Ventru - Dominate and Presence, while protected by Fortitude? It is not about whether he will win, but how he wants to win.<br /> <br /> Malkav - this one is terrifying, as he has three mental Disciplines. Each of the Mages could be subjected to a separate kind of torment for challenging him.<br /> <br /> Set - considering his occult and mystical inclinations, Mages should be wary of challenging him. He might have particularly strong mystical protections or be guarded by dark Spirits, for example. And his Disciplines all taken into account provide very strong protections.<br /> <br /> (I think that he is not an Antediluvian, but still interesting to consider)<br /> Tremere - considering he was the foremost Certamen duelist in the Order of Hermes, founded the House Tremere, is the leader of Clan Tremere, and as a Kindred has access to Auspex and Dominate...it also seems a folly to challenge him.<br /> <br /> Why do your poor Mages consider fighting an Antediluvian? Can't it be done otherwise? Combating their influence, trying to dismantle their plots? If anything, maybe attacking one while she or he is resting has some sense? Though this is probably asking to be killed or captured, as well - a resting place of Antediluvian likely has protections and guardians. And she or he just might wake up ; they are several ways for a Kindred to overcome the lessened ability to act during the day. And even with lesser capabilities, an Antediluvian might just have enough potency to fight off an attack by Mages.<br /> Various quests and undertakings to gather means, items, knowledge, and power to challenge an Antediluvian directly could be attempted...but considering who they are, would any Mage want to risk it? An Antediluvian could come to know about it, after all...<br /> <br /> Maybe it is that Antediluvians are not so personally potent, but this is how I see them. And even under the assumption that they are not that mystically and physically powerful, they still have their superb mastery of Disciplines to rely on for protection.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462901-build-a-mage-to-fight-an-antediluvian?p=1462951#post1462951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Corr2, Matter 2, you can teleport an object (to Set).</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, this is an idea. Teleport some nice and interesting object(s) to an Antediluvian as a gift and homage so she or he might just not bother the Mage(s). And the Sphere requirements are rather low in regard to this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-10-2021, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T10:02:34-07:00","id":1463322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462901-build-a-mage-to-fight-an-antediluvian?p=1463310#post1463310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fight an Antediluvian? Not try to combat Antediluvian's influence, plots, or their agents, not try to stalk an Antediluvian in their place of rest (also a folly, I'll come back to this later), but try to fight one directly? Oh dear, I just think this cannot work. The way I see it, the original 3rd Generation Founders just have this privilege that they cannot be simply harmed directly, except by each other. Their physical bodies are too resistant, their mysticism too potent, and their combat stats (including regeneration ability) are too high. Even battle forms of Mages (be it the mystical ones Tradition have listed or Hard Suits of the Technocracy) are simply not powerful enough.<br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> Maybe it is that Antediluvians aren't so personally potent, but this is how I see them. And even under the assumption that they are not that mystically and physically powerful, they still have their superb mastery of Disciplines to rely on for protection.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the above hits on what some people have said about how subjective this matter is. In some people's interpretation of the setting, the Antediluvians are truly invulnerable to any kind of mortal interference. Not my preferred interpretation, but a common one, especially from a Vampire-centric perspective. Arguably not a reasonable one from a Mage-centric perspective, but it's ultimately a Storyteller thing.<br /> <br /> But divine plot armour aside, most of the rest of what Muad'Dib says is legit. You're talking about going up against beings that will likely have 6+ in their dump stats, capable of pumping various stats even higher, with most or all of them likely having high levels in a Discipline that includes Storyteller-fiat precognition (assuming they don't have the high level powers allowing full-blown future-sight). And they should, reasonably, be played capable of using those abilities with terrifying effectiveness, since we are talking about beings that have survived thousands of years of covert warfare, the Jyhad. They should be as paranoid as any Mage, if not more so, with defences and contingency plans prepared for any threat that they can conceive of.<br /> <br /> The one canon example that we have of something going toe to toe with an Antediluvian involved a hypertech anti-magic nuclear bombardment as an opening salvo, followed by concentrated sunlight. And that was an Antediluvian that had presumably gone too mad to use its abilities to full effect.<br /> <br /> So the best answer to the question is probably a combination of thwarting the awareness of a paranoid demigod and then dropping every bit of force that you can onto its resting place at high noon, hopefully cracking its haven open like an egg so that the sunlight will hopefully finish the job for you. Arguably with step 3 being preventing any escape plans it has put into place for this kind of scenario from working.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T11:29:49-07:00","id":1463331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462901-build-a-mage-to-fight-an-antediluvian?p=1463310#post1463310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it is that Antediluvians are not so personally potent, but this is how I see them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a valid interpretation, but otherwise your love letter for the Antes ignore the actual content of the opening post.<br /> <br /> Antediluvians may be that powerful. Or not. So what really counts is how the ST will interpret them.<br /> <br /> Your every question is answered in the post. It is a &quot;high-level&quot; mixed game. The vampire characters are 4th gen with at least one 9th level Discipline each. The char in discussion have Arete 8 and one Arch-level Sphere. The chronicle run for years and the group is used to this style of play. Chatting with Antes is already <i>par for the course</i> for them. This fight, if it happens, will be the culmination of their run-ins with Sutekh.<br /> <br /> Whatever our individual interpretations of what the Antes are, they are utterly irrelevant here. OP already knows how their ST does it and the battle is feasible. There will be no Plot Armor and no Transcendental Powers, at least to the point of making the clash impossible. Whatever we think of such a power level of play is equally meaningless, this is not about your table or my table.<br /> <br /> But yeah, this will be an extremely tough one, I think this is pretty much a consensus. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> I wouldn't expect less than 6 dots in dump stats and at least 3 Disciplines in a whopping 10, which is pretty rad. I wouldn't be surprised with at least 2 others at this level, 1 of them a Setite Sorcery Path, maybe more. No build will be single-handedly able to deal with that, but they won't be alone in the fight and the group already knows what's coming, so preparation, preparation, preparation.<br /> <br /> My full expectation is that they'll all die, but have a nice hardcore tale to tell from beyond the Shroud in their upcoming Wraith game. But they do have a chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T12:07:42-07:00","id":1463336,"title":"","content":"Lets not completely disregard how much ST fiat BS archmasters are supposed to be able to do even if you have to take Master of the Art into account.<br /> <br /> For better or worse, we also know more about what the archmasters can do simply because some of them are active in the stories.<br /> <br /> Can Voormas take on an Antedeluvian head on? Who even knows. Should an Antedeluvian trust in their supreme power here? Hell no. The ones with precognition would know to be scared as hell of Voormas because he can take out anything less than an Antedeluvian, and killing him isn't actually possible without the Knife of Ixion; he's even better at body swapping to a new one if his current one dies than they are. He's trying to kill death itself... and has the power to succeed. That's not a package to take lightly.<br /> <br /> Does an Antedeluvian want to trust in their supernaturally tough bodies against someone like Porthos? He can turn the space around them into the surface of the sun. He's not a walking nuke, he's a walking nuke firing submarine with the implied range (just ask the survivors of the Technocratic attack on Doissetep). He's technically weaker than Voormas too (more Arete, lower Spheres).<br /> <br /> And the set up in the OP is a cabal of archmages, not just one.<br /> <br /> So lets not sell the mages too short here since they're in highly subjective power territory as well.<br /> <br /> Of course, PCs mean rules. The difference in power between an archmage with Time 4 an without Time 4 is ridiculous because of the hanging effects ability that comes with it. Similarly Prime 4 and being good at Wonder crafting. Because both of these let mages screw with action economy and magic. Time 4 lets you prep spells ahead of time so you can put reflexive triggers on them rather than needing an action to cast a spell, and Prime 4 plus lots of time means you can afford to craft Wonders that can cast magic on their own, letting you cast multiple time in the same turn.<br /> <br /> So the point of &quot;don't give mages time to prep&quot; is still very important even at this level of play.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T14:29:50-07:00","id":1463348,"title":"","content":"I definitely agree that the party seems to be at the 'level' for the task; they probably don't individually add up to Porthos or Voormas, but collectively they seem capable in theory. But that's why a lot of what I mentioned had to do with their awareness and escape plans. If the Antediluvian in question has reason to suspect that they might be a threat, then they will probably make themselves as scarce as possible while engaging in a proxy war through their minions. I think that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> is right that information-gathering and counter-intelligence are as important a part of this as the raw firepower, because an Antediluvian isn't going to get in a fair fight with someone that has the raw power to bring them down, so the party needs the means of setting the confrontation on their terms, whatever those may be.<br /> <br /> The fact that we know we're dealing with Set tells us a bit more about the situation. As noted above, one of the masters of Obfuscate is going to be extremely difficult to target. Set is also an extremely powerful sorcerer, which means he's likely to be better defended against more esoteric forms of attack than some of the other Antediluvians. One possible upside is that he's not necessarily going to have the highest levels of Auspex, assuming all of them focus most of all on their Clan Disciplines. And they are at a bit of a disadvantage in that it sounds like there has been an ongoing antagonism in their relationship with Set, which puts them &quot;on his radar&quot; and justifies the Storyteller having them under observation. And they might be the target of a pre-emptive strike if Set suspects them of plotting against him.<br /> <br /> Going back to the discussion of how rules are on the table, one of the big questions is how the Storyteller will interpret the power of Level 10 Disciplines. To a lesser extent, I don't know if they ever put down in writing what an Antediluvian's max Blood Pool is; the charts in the Core Rulebook always leave it a mystery IIRC. Depending on how the Storyteller chooses to rule Level 10 Disciplines and their costs could have a lot of influence on how a head-on conflict with an Antediluvian could go. In contrast, the rules for Archmages are a bit more concrete, though I'm not super familiar with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T14:56:18-07:00","id":1463350,"title":"","content":"To the last point first: there's actually three different rules for archmages. (1) There's just a 6th level and you enter ST fiat levels of power (2) there's a whole 6-9 level to each Sphere like Elder Disciplines and (3) there isn't even a 6th dot, archmages are just a combination of high levels of Spheres, experience, and magical resources, to the point of being ST fiat level powerful if prepped.<br /> <br /> This all due to the fact that #3 was going to be the original intent, but someone gave Porthos Forces 6. Went detailing what that meant, #1 became the default. Later, to make archmages more playable, #2 was introduced in Masters of the Art following the model of Elder Disciplines. Revised kinda kept clear of taking a position using the Avatar Storm to make the archmages a non-issue, though the Revised stat block on Voormas has him with Entropy 7 implying that MotA is still official. M20 has stated that #3 is the basic stance of the game now, and isn't going to support 1 or 2.<br /> <br /> Also, in terms of adding up to Porthos, his Spheres are: Correspondence 4, Entropy 5, Forces 6, Life 4, Mind 5, Matter 3, Prime 5, Spirit 4, Time 3. Plus Avatar 5, and his real big thing: Arete 9. That's not actually that much more powerful than the suggested stats in the OP:<br /> <br /> &quot;Maybe assume 1 6 dot sphere, 2-3 5 dot spheres, 1-2 4 dot spheres. And Arete, Avatar 7+.&quot;<br /> <br /> He has one 6, three 5s, three 4s instead of two, and two 3s. His Arete is obviously way above 7, but for instant casting it's just two more dice. It's rituals where he's going to over power them individual with multiple rules and more rolls possible in a ritual. Avatar 5 is actually below, but also not that relevant in at the 5+ level to a mage with Prime.<br /> <br /> So, sure, they PCs are right on Porthos's level but they're pretty close, and as I noted before, them being a cabal is a huge advantage if they can leverage it properly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T16:20:50-07:00","id":1463353,"title":"","content":"This continues to be a great thread. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> nails the &quot;set-up&quot;.<br /> <br /> I guess to clarify and be more specific. We have encountered Set and had direct interaction with him. He is currently imprisoned in some sort of extra-dimension (possibly within the duat). Since we have been there, we may be able to go there again via the same channel. Saulot directly told us that Set was pissed at us. Probably because we killed a slew of ancient Settites who were in torpor. We also manipulated one of his childer, who was then sent to kill us but whom we killed instead. <br /> <br /> My character:<br /> * 8 Arete, 8 Avater, 6 Prime, 5 Spirit, 4 Mind, 3 Correspondence, 3 Life, 3 Forces, 2 Time, 2 Matter, 2 Entropy<br /> * Saulot has spent a significant amount of time with our coterie, including passing his memories to my character (while we are not entirely canon, we believe he is about to confront the tremere and knows what's going to happen / has a plan). I would say he is a strong ally.<br /> * Only major merit is Nephilim, which we've interpreted to basically inherit a downsized Demon template without the actual powers without the Lore stuff. (It also means he cannot become a ghoul or be blood bound as vampire blood is rendered inert if he consumes it.) It comes with other mental protections.<br /> * Our mage mechanics are... favorable. I am only mildly constrained by paradigm and foci and can effectively &quot;fast cast&quot; almost anything. <br /> * Avatar 8 and the ST seems to be hinting that my avatar may be Dwojti, which seems... insane.<br /> <br /> Of important note, one of the vampires is a True Brujah and has Temporis 9. He also has some insane magical sword that was an in game gift from his sire and he has become the de facto killing machine in the group. Another vampire has lower disciplines but well developed crowd control mechanisms.<br /> <br /> Again, I will add the disclaimer that I know some people will think this is power gaming or bonkers, but this has mostly happened organically. We played for almost a year as mortals and all of us thought we would be vampires. The ST put me on the mage path and all this stuff has evolved in the story. And while I have played a limited amount of mage before, this is definitely the deepest I've been.<br /> <br /> So I guess my revised or follow-up questions:<br /> <br /> * Given all of that, where would you spend XP? (This is not a fast XP game, so this shit does take forever.) I currently have 8 XP and Mind is my 7xp sphere, so I am thinking of going for Mind 5 next and then I am not sure. Like I'd probably go for Time 4 for to get contingent effects but don't want to step on the Trujah's domain.<br /> <br /> * How would you think about research and preparation for this? I have a few allies (Balthazaar a powerful hermetic mage / one of the wise men who trained me, a ferryman ally, a fuck ton of powerful vampires, etc.) but trying to figure out what I should try to dig up.<br /> <br /> * Any wonders/items/etc that I should consider crafting? For me or for the vampires?<br /> <br /> * Any thoughts on strategy for such an engagement would be awesome.<br /> <br /> Other notes:<br /> <br /> * I doubt we are going to decide to seek out and try to kill Set anytime soon, but if it becomes increasingly clear he is after us I think being proactive is probably better than waiting for him to get free and choose the battle.<br /> <br /> * While we haven't exactly gone out of our way to start a battle with him, we've probably done more than enough to incite it. We're also pretty actively fighting on the side of Hardestat and others before the formation of the Camarilla against Tzimisce and maybe House Tremere. We have also been actively fighting Baali and infernalists for a long time and are constantly digging deeper into their &quot;organization&quot;. So I'm pretty sure if it's not Set, we're eventually going to get into a direct fight with an antediluvian or something similar.<br /> <br /> Thanks again for all the input and thoughts, this is amazing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26423-lokitx","name":"LokiTX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T04:21:40-07:00","id":1463693,"title":"","content":"Is throwing them into the abyss an option? Because if so you could just defeat them with spirit, and I guess time to just be quicker then them.<br /> <br /> Though also flinging them into any realm is just as good as the Abyss. If you want to be super fancy you could make your own horizon realm to kill them.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, if you had high corr you could just... catapult them into the sun.<br /> <br /> they're just vampires. I'd choose methods they can't counter with disaplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25510,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25510-jasper-mage","user":"Jasper mage","date":". 10-13-2021, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25510-jasper-mage","name":"Jasper mage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T06:34:02-07:00","id":1463700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiTX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462901-build-a-mage-to-fight-an-antediluvian#post1462901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am in a long running WOD campaign that is a mix of mage and vampire PCs. Everyone is powerful. (IE: 4th gen vampires, archmages) - this has been running for years and we started as humans. I'm a mage. We have encountered two antediluvians in our travels and the coterie/cabal/whatever has a pretty good relationship with one and an escalating relationship with the other (Set, who is... currently not able to take direct actions). I think we are about to tangle with others or see changes as we are approaching the time of the Camarilla / Tremere / etc. It's in the 1100s.<br /> <br /> Anyway, forgetting for a moment whether you think this is insane or not (it's fun, we've played together for 20 years, so we're ok with this game structure which would obviously be OP/nuts for others)...<br /> <br /> How would you build a mage to fight an antediluvian?<br /> <br /> The following special advantages exist:<br /> * Paradox is extremely low in this time period / environment.<br /> * Fast casting / on the fly casting is largely possible. (This is a pretty loose interpretation of the mage rules..)<br /> * Maybe assume 1 6 dot sphere, 2-3 5 dot spheres, 1-2 4 dot spheres. And Arete, Avatar 7+.<br /> <br /> I have Arete 8. There will likely be several vampires with 1-2 disciplines in the 8-9 range in the fight. If we are forced to fight an antediluvian it will likely be Set, although Tremere and Tzimisce are also possible.<br /> <br /> I am not sure we can win, so the strategy might also be a fight to escape / stalemate / imprison.<br /> <br /> Looking forward to your thoughts!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I have <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383952-v20-antediluvians-peach#post1383952\">made up stats for Giovanni and Tzimisce</a> (based on the existing stats on Giovanni Chronicles and Gehenna) that would give you an idea of the power range Antediluvians should have <b><i><u>at the very least</u></i></b>, Giovanni is the weakest of the Antes, and Tzimisce is at, or near the top. Again, my post has the <b><i><u>minimum</u></i></b> those creatures should have.<ul><li>If we count the Level 10 discipline plot device power, then the true way to kill an antediluvian involves Time + Entropy to find out what it could do given a particular action from your side. Just iterate timelines until you find out what it can do, and what it sticks to kill them.</li> <li>If we go for the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411167-all-level-10-disciplines-rituals-and-their-resources?p=1411168#post1411168\">specific Level 10 powers</a>, then as long as you keep your distance you are golden<b><u><i>*</i></u></b>, you can go the &quot;<i>create/summon sunlight/fire around it for hours</i>&quot; route, that kills all but Tzimisce with its Reform Body (you need to trap him somewhere impossible to escape with Vampiric powers, Deep Umbra for example).</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b><u><i>*</i></u>Going by rules as written, Correspondence 3 + Prime 2 + Forces 3 ought to kill all of them. Summon sunlight/fire and hit them, Correspondence is the power that vampires have the least chance of emulating, so nothing fancy, just use aggravated remote distance damage.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 10-27-2022, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T09:47:43-07:00","id":1463712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jasper mage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462901-build-a-mage-to-fight-an-antediluvian?p=1463693#post1463693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they're just vampires. I'd choose methods they can't counter with disaplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're clearly not used to Vampire Storytellers. Or to Vampire in any dept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T10:53:54-07:00","id":1463723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462901-build-a-mage-to-fight-an-antediluvian?p=1463331#post1463331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a valid interpretation, but otherwise your love letter for the Antes ignore the actual content of the opening post.<br /> (...)<br /> Whatever our individual interpretations of what the Antes are, they are utterly irrelevant here. OP already knows how their ST does it and the battle is feasible. There will be no Plot Armor and no Transcendental Powers, at least to the point of making the clash impossible. Whatever we think of such a power level of play is equally meaningless, this is not about your table or my table.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, I did ignore the perspective of the OP. I'm thinking that these Sphere Effects could be very useful if capable and experienced Mages would have to directly fight an Antediluvian...<br /> <br /> Correspondence 4 - multiple co-locations to confuse as to who is the real one. Possibly with an invisibility Effect added to the real Mage so that the Vampire is led into surely hitting a co-location.<br /> Forces 3 - could be used to create illusions of Mages or dangers<br /> Correspondence 5 - I have this notion of using a confusing co-located area to gain an advantage. Possibly creating surroundings which can only be perceived correctly and navigated with Correspondence or Matter senses.<br /> A co-located area could also be used as prison, most likely a temporary one.<br /> Time 5 - gives the possibility of moving out of time while everything else stays still. It is not said if Magick can be cast, but strategizing and general preparations could be done. Or a tactical retreat.<br /> Time 3 or Time 5 - Rewinding Time<br /> Time 5 - shunting wounds or results of attacks into the future<br /> Time 2 - thicken the walls of time to counter the divinations of an Antediluvian<br /> Time 4 - A Mind 3-5 telepathic assault hanged in preparation<br /> Entropy 4 - a combat Blessing can be cast so the fight turns in the favor of Mages<br /> Entropy 5 - a blessing could protect the minds of Mages and their allies, and help they overcome fear or doubts<br /> Entropy 5 - an Affect Thought of doubt, hesitation, fear, or overconfidence could be attempted<br /> Prime 4 or Matter 3 to destroy or disenchant magic and mundane items<br /> Prime - some mystical shield to counter Disciplines or Blood Sorcery in general<br /> Life 5 - a resurrection or reforging the body spell to give Mages more chances<br /> <br /> In regard to physically attacking Antediluvians, I think simply using Forces would be most effective. Or possibly Entropy. Life or Prime just do not feel right for the task.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-13-2021, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T14:17:59-07:00","id":1463883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462901-build-a-mage-to-fight-an-antediluvian?p=1463712#post1463712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're clearly not used to Vampire Storytellers. Or to Vampire in any dept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've run VtM many times.<br /> <br /> admittedly I've not played with many high level disaplines. but one thing vampires generally lack is teleportation and umbral travel. unless they're battling lasombra with his abyss stuff or giovanni with his necromancy, I don't see why shunting an antedeliuvian somewhere else isn't the obvious winner. besides that it might be a little anti climatic. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25510-jasper-mage","name":"Jasper mage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T15:18:45-07:00","id":1463890,"title":"","content":"Auspex is a common Discipline and well below Elder levels lets vampires project their minds out of their bodies. Multiple Antes are noted as having moved their souls to a new host and are no longer in their original body.<br /> <br /> So it really isn't that hard to imagine most of them can easily overcome this sort of tactic.<br /> <br /> Again, remember that the Antes have &quot;whatever the plot demands,&quot; powers at their disposal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T15:52:17-07:00","id":1463895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462901-build-a-mage-to-fight-an-antediluvian?p=1463890#post1463890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, remember that the Antes have &quot;whatever the plot demands,&quot; powers at their disposal.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> This is the reason I suggested Entropy + Time to iterate along timelines, to findout what they could do vs your attacks, and what will really kill them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T15:52:58-07:00","id":1463897,"title":"","content":"Not to mention that Sorcery Disciplines have lots of answers to common vulnerabilities in a splat crossover, including counterspell, or access to simpler answers like Awakened minions and Wonders.<br /> <br /> A fight with any &quot;high-level&quot; member of any splat will never be that straightforward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T16:03:07-07:00","id":1463899,"title":"","content":"There's also been a bunch of crossover rules over the editions that blunt the power of mages (esp. if they're behind in the biggest number of dots contest). The M20 rules that let any supernatural counter-spell Awakened magic means an Ante's likely to have a lot more dice to do that than the mage will to cast it (at least against instant casting).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T10:24:35-07:00","id":1464208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462901-build-a-mage-to-fight-an-antediluvian?p=1463336#post1463336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets not completely disregard how much ST fiat BS archmasters are supposed to be able to do even if you have to take Master of the Art into account.<br /> <br /> For better or worse, we also know more about what the archmasters can do simply because some of them are active in the stories.<br /> <br /> Can Voormas take on an Antedeluvian head on? Who even knows. Should an Antedeluvian trust in their supreme power here? Hell no. The ones with precognition would know to be scared as hell of Voormas because he can take out anything less than an Antedeluvian, and killing him isn't actually possible without the Knife of Ixion; he's even better at body swapping to a new one if his current one dies than they are. He's trying to kill death itself... and has the power to succeed. That's not a package to take lightly.<br /> <br /> Does an Antedeluvian want to trust in their supernaturally tough bodies against someone like Porthos? He can turn the space around them into the surface of the sun. He's not a walking nuke, he's a walking nuke firing submarine with the implied range (just ask the survivors of the Technocratic attack on Doissetep). He's technically weaker than Voormas too (more Arete, lower Spheres).</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought about an Order of Hermes Archmage or Voormas when I first read this topic. And it does seem epic and intriguing, the idea of a supreme and exemplary Mage (or a group of such Mages) taking on an Antediluvian (or one of the ancient Methuselahs), channeling all sorts of potent Magicks while doing so. After all, aren't Mages the persons who know the secrets of reality, and search for the ultimate truths? <a href=\"https://ibb.co/WHCNxvT\" target=\"_blank\">https://ibb.co/WHCNxvT</a> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/cryKByt\" target=\"_blank\">https://ibb.co/cryKByt</a> (pictures from 1st Edition Corebook) And it is a special kind of triumph to bring down a Vampire who would probably think of a Mage as a mere mortal spellcaster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-16-2021, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}